omment-1691900504","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2091","id":1691900504,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85k2FpY","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-08-24T15:28:49Z","updated_at":"2023-08-24T15:28:49Z","body":"So here's a question:\r\n\r\n* SWI-exception permits the exception to apply if you link the software together with files compiled with any \"Free Software compiler.\"\r\n* By contrast, this one only permits the exception to apply if the compiler was a \"GNU compiler.\"\r\n\r\nI'd tend to treat these as substantively different. This isn't a situation where e.g. the difference is in determining which files or content the exception applies to; rather, the difference is in the legal effect of the exception's scope. I'd think this is different enough to warrant a separate exception identifier (which I'd be +1 for adding as a separate ID).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1691900504/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hoora